// Two sparks whose rings interfere where they meet.
name Twin Sparks
rule B1/S
steps 3
hint Two sparks. Where their rings would overlap, the cells had too many neighbours to be born. An ember drifts along the row below them: cross once it has passed.
tip Two sparks, six cells apart. The rings that would have touched lost their touching columns.
intro Two sparks, close enough to touch. Where they would have met, nothing was born at all. And something still moves down here: an ember of the old growth, drifting along its row. It burns what it touches.
outro Too many neighbours and the birth does not happen. Loneliness was the law.
